\begin_layout Section*
But first,
 typing
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If we want to learn programming by numbers,
 we need to know how to write them.
 I’ve briefly discussed this before—
every language has its own way,
 and some even use 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "sigils"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/p/the-summoning-of-spirits"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\begin_inset script superscript

\begin_layout Plain Layout
⌘
\end_layout

\end_inset

  Here are some examples of numbers in Zyzyxia:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
42
\family default
 —
 an integer,
 
\family typewriter
INT
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
42.0
\family default
 —
 a fixed-point number (alternatively 
\family typewriter
4.20e1
\family default
),
 
\family typewriter
FIX
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
42~
\family default
 —
 a floating-point number,
 
\family typewriter
FLOAT
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
:42
\family default
 —
 a Small integer,
 
\family typewriter
SMALL
\family default
,
 useful for numbers in the (range] of 
\begin_inset Formula $\pm231$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The trick with Zyzyxia is that she uses strong typing:
 so if you want to 
\family typewriter
ADD
\family default
 say 
\family typewriter
42
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
:42
\family default
,
 you must explicitly say either 
\family typewriter
ADD 42 INT :42
\family default
,
 or 
\family typewriter
ADD SMALL 42 :42
\family default
.
 Otherwise,
 you’ll get an error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We supplement these with two other ‘types of things’.
 One is just # —
 a symbol for ‘null’;
 the other,
 ‘Empty’ is made up of two underscores __ .
 For example 
\family typewriter
( 1 2 # 3 )
\family default
 represents a list with the third element set to null,
 but we may also want to use __ to signify that the element at position 5 “doesn’t even exist”.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\family typewriter
NULL #
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
NULL __
\family default
 both return 
\family typewriter
Yes
\family default
;
 
\family typewriter
EQ __
\family default
 only returns 
\family typewriter
Yes
\family default
 if its second argument is also __.
\end_layout

